        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "936835ac-a7a9-5bb4-b1fc-19eef436d2ab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Leonotis, Psychopsis, Leonotis artemisia\n- Plant families: Lamiaceae, Orchidaceae\n- Places: Northern South America, Central America, Trinidad\n- Topics: flowering plants, horticultural abbreviations, plant taxonomy\n\nFacts:\n- Leonotis is a genus of flowering plants in the family Lamiaceae.\n- Psychopsis is a genus of five known orchid species native to northern South America, Central America, and Trinidad.\n- Psychopsis is abbreviated as Psychp in the horticultural trade.\n- Leonotis artemisia is a species in the genus Leonotis and the family Lamiaceae.\n- Leonotis artemisia is also known as motherwort.",
